}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/65/65a76a438b3459a92db0e00b0c9bd281b8a9c58fa68afd2d8e6468a1d99b1cf9.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1f1fe35-990c-50d4-ada2-aab504633e3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294964 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295013 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295013 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278477" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295013 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295013 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fb/fb178149bac4d1fcfd0690b7005f263c3647488ac86ed70f114